{{!--
    ui/setting-ref - reference link to a setting key in the API docs, shown at the
    top-right of config form fields (floated from sm up, on its own line below it):
      {{> ui/setting-ref name="proxyEnabled"}}
    Params:
      name   - settings key, shown as the link text (required)
      suffix - literal text after the link, e.g. suffix='="*"' (optional)
      href   - override link target (default: the Settings update operation in
               the bundled Swagger UI)
      plain  - true to render the name without a link (env-var refs that have
               no docs anchor)
      prefix - literal text inside the brackets before the link, e.g.
               prefix="API Reference: " (optional)
      nofloat - true to never float, at any width. For a stacked reference column,
               where a floated first entry lands on the same line as the
               right-aligned block under it and prints over it (optional)
      class  - extra classes on the wrapper, e.g. "whitespace-nowrap" to keep a
               setting key from breaking mid-identifier (optional)
    The float is sm-and-up only. A setting key is long and does not wrap, so beside a
    phone-width field it left the label a column of single words - or, where that field
    was a flex row the float could not narrow any further, printed on top of it. Below
    sm it takes its own line, right-aligned where the float put it.
--}}
<div class="text-base-content/60{{#unless nofloat}} sm:float-right max-sm:mb-0.5 max-sm:text-end{{/unless}} code-link{{#if class}} {{class}}{{/if}}">[{{prefix}}{{#if plain}}{{name}}{{else}}<a
        href="{{#if href}}{{href}}{{else}}/admin/reference/settings#postV1Settings{{/if}}" target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link link-animated">{{name}}</a>{{/if}}{{suffix}}]</div>
